# Fetched corpus content — ~49MB, re-fetchable from raw/manifest.json.
# NOTE the trailing /* rather than /: git does not descend into an ignored
# DIRECTORY, so a negation below it can never match. Ignoring the CONTENTS is
# what makes the exception reachable.
packages/corpus/data/*
packages/corpus/raw/*
# ...except the CHECKOUT LOCK. The comment above has always said the corpus is
# "re-fetchable from raw/manifest.json" — but `packages/corpus/raw/` (with the
# trailing slash this file's own note warns against, four lines up) ignored the
# directory, so the manifest went with it and a fresh clone had nothing to fetch
# FROM. It pins a url and a commit SHA per checkout: our metadata about third-party
# repositories, not their content, so tracking it redistributes nothing. It is what
# `pnpm --filter @golem/corpus bootstrap` reads.
!packages/corpus/raw/manifest.json
# ...and the HUGGING FACE lock, for the same reason and on the same terms. It pins each
# harvested dataset by url + commit SHA, and records the sources that were fetched, read and
# REFUSED with the grounds for refusing. The chunks it produces stay ignored (they are a build
# artefact, like chunks.jsonl); this is the metadata that makes the harvest reproducible and
# the refusals reviewable, so a source cannot quietly change under the product.
!packages/corpus/raw/manifest.hf.json
# ...except the source LEDGER. sources.json is 0.4MB of derived provenance and
# licence verdicts, and §H requires that metadata be preserved rather than
# regenerated on demand — a classification nobody can diff is one nobody reviews.
!packages/corpus/data/sources.json
!packages/corpus/data/registries.json
# The ContentRecord ledger: which sources are one idea, which diverged. Small, because the
# per-file hashes it derives from are regenerable and are not persisted.
!packages/corpus/data/content.json
# The registry handoff: 1,082 resolvable candidates. Tracked so `discover --includeRegistry`
# works without re-cloning 43MB of package indexes first.
!packages/corpus/data/registry-seeds.json
packages/evals/results/raw/

# Playwright
test-results/
playwright-report/

# Throwaway measurement scaffolding
measure-tmp.mjs

# Agent worktrees — isolated checkouts, never part of the committed tree
.claude/worktrees/

# Training: local venv, model weights, datasets and adapters. Re-buildable from
# src/build-dataset.mjs + the pinned corpus manifest; none of it belongs in git.
packages/training/.venv/
packages/training/adapters/
packages/training/mlxdata/

# THE TRAINING ARTEFACTS: large and derived are ignored, small and CITED are not.
#
# runs/ and data/ were ignored wholesale alongside adapters/, and adapters/ is 210 MB of
# safetensors so that rule is right for it. runs/ is 36 KB of plain-text logs, and four backlog
# rows cite those logs as their only evidence — so ignoring them meant four rows nobody but the
# machine that ran the training could ever verify. That is collateral from a rule aimed at
# something else.
#
# data/ stays ignored because train/val/test.jsonl are DERIVED — build-dataset.mjs regenerates
# them — but dataset-card.json is 8 KB, is cited by a row, and is the provenance record for a
# dataset that is not itself tracked. It is re-included by name.
packages/training/data/*
!packages/training/data/dataset-card.json
packages/training/mlxdata-text/
packages/training/mlxdata/

# nonstop (machine-specific)
.claude/settings.local.json
.nonstop/

# unlazy Stop hook session state — machine-specific, and tracking it makes every tree dirty
.unlazy-hook-state.json
.unlazy/

# Pixel frames are written on every check-pixels run and a full capture is ~21MB. The BASELINE is
# committed, because a regression is measured against it, and §16.10 wants the final pass's capture
# committed as evidence. Interim captures are local: they exist to be looked at, not to be carried
# in history. They are ignored rather than deleted — §18 forbids discarding an untracked path, and
# a frame somebody is mid-way through reviewing is exactly the kind of thing that rule protects.
docs/evidence/pixels/*
!docs/evidence/pixels/baseline/
!docs/evidence/pixels/final/

# graphify's generated map. `graphify update .` rewrites graph.json (6MB), graph.html and an AST
# cache on every run, and nothing in this repository reads any of it — checked with grep across
# scripts/, apps/*/src, tests/ and packages/*/src before ignoring it. Tracking it meant a ~12MB
# diff per rebuild for an artifact that regenerates from source in about a minute.
#
# GRAPH_REPORT.md stays tracked: it is small, it is the part a person reads, and its "built from
# commit" line is what tells you the rest is stale.
graphify-out/*
!graphify-out/GRAPH_REPORT.md
handoff/
